  "modeldesc-skeleton": "Animated human skeleton.",
  "modeldesc-skeleton-cosmetic": "Animated human skeleton.",
  "modeldesc-infected": "<font color=\"#99c9f9\"><i>You remember nothing of your early years - you have lived far too long. Yet faint echoes remain from the time when you were still part of the being that grew these bones. At first, you slowly took control; later, the remaining flesh decayed and fell away. Now only bones remain - and you dwell within them, having made them your home.</i></font><br/><br/>A human skeleton occupied by a parasitic creature that infected its host while still alive. Originating from the same source as rot and rust, it is mostly unaffected by temporal instability. The parasite's small body stores little energy, but it also requires less food to sustain itself.",
  "modeldesc-possessed": "<font color=\"#99c9f9\"><i>These are your bones - always were. They are all that remain of your former life, when all else died, decayed, and the old world crumbled to ruin. Your memories fade with each passing year, save for one: the agony that ended your life, and the hatred for the world that brought it upon you.</i></font><br/><br/>A skeleton possessed by the ghost of the human to whom these bones once belonged. The spirit needs neither food nor breath and feels no cold, but it is temporally unstable - constantly losing stability and requiring temporal gears to survive.",
  "modeldesc-reanimated": "<font color=\"#99c9f9\"><i>You were risen and bound by unknown magic. Remembrance of hunger drives you mad, undoing the spell that bound your bones and forcing you to seek human food.</i></font><br/><br/>A human skeleton reanimated through necromancy. It bears no true connection to the bones' former owner beyond the remains themselves. Its mind was shaped by magic to serve a purpose and obey its creator - yet the creator is long gone, and the skeleton now is free to roam the world.",

