  "game:characterdesc-skeletons-commoner": "<font color=\"#99c9f9\"><i>You remember nothing of your previous life. The only clue to who you once were are the shackles still clasped around your leg bones.</i></font>",
  "game:characterdesc-skeletons-archer": "<font color=\"#99c9f9\"><i>You remember how to draw a bow - but those memories are not your own. You feel that whatever raised you has planted them within you for a purpose.</i></font>",
  "game:characterdesc-skeletons-crossbowman": "<font color=\"#99c9f9\"><i>You remember how to load and fire a crossbow - but those memories are not your own. You feel that something which brought you back has gifted them to you for a reason.</i></font>",
  "game:characterdesc-skeletons-spearman": "<font color=\"#99c9f9\"><i>You remember how to thrust with a spear - but those memories are not your own. You feel that something which raised you bestowed them upon you with intent.</i></font>",
  "game:characterdesc-skeletons-swordsman": "<font color=\"#99c9f9\"><i>You remember how to wield a sword - but those memories are not your own. You feel they were placed within you by the one who raised you, for reasons unknown to you.</i></font>",
  "game:characterdesc-skeletons-smith": "<font color=\"#99c9f9\"><i>You recall fragments of another life - a smith, a bowyer, a tailor... Then realization strikes: these are not your memories. They were placed within you for a purpose.</i></font>",
  "game:characterdesc-skeletons-infected-omnivore": "<font color=\"#99c9f9\"><i>You feed on whatever you can find. Hunger knows no bounds for you.</i></font>",
  "game:characterdesc-skeletons-infected-carnivore": "<font color=\"#99c9f9\"><i>You crave flesh to feel satiated. The instincts of a hunter linger in your bones.</i></font>",
  "game:characterdesc-skeletons-infected-herbivore": "<font color=\"#99c9f9\"><i>You require plants to feel satiated. The habits of a forager remain etched into your being.</i></font>",
  "game:characterdesc-skeletons-possessed-oathbreaker": "<font color=\"#99c9f9\"><i>You once swore to come to your allies' aid, but when the time came, you fled and hid in the mountain pass. Your body starved to death, yet your ghost remained - bound by the oath you once gave.</i></font>",
  "game:characterdesc-skeletons-possessed-tortured": "<font color=\"#99c9f9\"><i>You were a lord captured in battle by a pretender to your throne - your sworn enemy. Imprisoned within your own castle, you were tortured until nothing but hatred remained. When your mangled body died, your ghost endured, seeking vengeance.</i></font>",
  "game:characterdesc-skeletons-possessed-burntlive": "<font color=\"#99c9f9\"><i>You were a priest, sickened by the greed and corruption of your superiors. You spoke out against their excess, and then they came for you. After days of torture, you were burned alive at the stake. Your body turned to ash, but your hatred endured, binding your ghost to the bones.</i></font>",
  "game:characterdesc-skeletons-possessed-traitor": "<font color=\"#99c9f9\"><i>You were a scout in an army sworn to defend your homeland from invaders. When captured, you betrayed your people under the threat of torture - but they tortured you anyway and left your body to rot unburied. Your flesh decayed, but your guilt chained your ghost to the bones.</i></font>",
  "game:characterdesc-skeletons-possessed-inventor": "<font color=\"#99c9f9\"><i>Once you were a tinkerer, a smith, an inventor. You delved deep into the unknown, helping to create the Machine meant to save the world - but it brought only destruction. Your body perished, yet your guilt endures, binding your ghost to what remained.</i></font>",

